<title>MEXICO: POLL- Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 18.45 pct.</title>
<headline>POLL- Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 18.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 75 basis points to 18.45 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     17.70	    18.45		   + 75 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     19.00	    19.16		   + 16 bps</p>
<p>    181-DAY    20.25	    20.34		   +  9 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     20.24	    20.44		   + 20 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((-Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
